              "id": "39133002"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Catalyzes the dephosphorylation of pyridoxal-phosphate (PLP) (PubMed:15808744, PubMed:16990279, PubMed:39133002). Shows a broad substrate specificity in vitro, as it can hydrolyze a wide range of phosphorylated metabolites, including PLP, erythrose-4-phosphate (Ery4P), fructose-1,6-bis-phosphate (Fru1,6bisP), FMN, acetyl-phosphate, carbamoyl-phosphate, imido-di-phosphate and the artificial chromogenic susbtrate, p-nitrophenyl phosphate (pNPP) (PubMed:15808744, PubMed:16990279). Shows also weak activity with pyridoxine phosphate (PNP), but it plays only a minor role in PNP homeostasis (PubMed:39133002)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
